 `createRentalService()` (exported from `src/index.ts`) returns an in-memory rental service:
 
-- `addEquipment({ id, kind, dailyPrice })` registers a `'board'` or `'sail'`; `dailyPrice` is an integer
-  number of euro cents per day.
+- `addEquipment({ id, kind, dailyPrice, hourlyPrice? })` registers a `'board'` or `'sail'`; `dailyPrice` is an
+  integer number of euro cents per day and the optional `hourlyPrice` the same per hour.
 - `quote({ itemId, start, end })` returns `{ itemId, start, end, total }`.
 - `book({ itemId, start, end })` books the item and returns `{ id, itemId, start, end, total }`.
 
@@ -25,5 +25,11 @@ of the period.
 period; `kind` is optional and, when omitted, every kind is considered. It throws for a period that is not
 whole days or an unknown kind. An item booked for any part of the period is not listed.
 
+Hourly rental: a rental shorter than a day whose `start` and `end` are on the hour (UTC) costs the item's
+`hourlyPrice` for each hour, with no long-stay reduction, e.g. `2026-07-01T13:00:00Z` to
+`2026-07-01T17:00:00Z` is four hours. An item without an `hourlyPrice` cannot be rented by the hour, so
+`quote` and `book` throw for it. A rental of a day or more must still be whole days, midnight to midnight.
+Hourly bookings block overlapping periods like any other; `availability` still takes whole days only.
+
 Cancellation (no refund under 24 hours before the start, full refund otherwise) is not
 implemented yet.
